    "body": "## Problem\r\n\r\n`nvim_strwidth()` ignores `String.size`, so a C/FFI caller measuring a slice gets the width of the full underlying string.\r\n\r\n## Solution\r\n\r\nMake a bounded copy before calling the existing grapheme-aware width routine. Return zero directly for empty slices. This preserves emoji/combining behavior while respecting the byte boundary.\r\n\r\nFixes #33836.\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- Fail-first FFI regression on master `298aea7382`\r\n- Every byte prefix of ASCII, wide characters, combining marks, VS16/ZWJ emoji, embedded NUL, and controls\r\n- Exact-sized non-NUL storage and NULL/empty input\r\n- FFI suite: 2 passed; existing width API tests: 3 passed\r\n- Debug build, C lint, StyLua, commit lint, and whitespace checks pass\r\n\r\nThe fix adds one temporary copy/allocation for nonempty inputs; a future bounded grapheme iterator could eliminate that cost. Local functional tests use stdio RPC with only the optional test-ID listener suppressed.\r\n\r\nAI-assisted.",
    "closed_at": null,
