            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Thanks. The helper matches the existing Unicode test cases. For an invalid byte `0x80`, though, it returns 4 while `nvim_strwidth` currently returns 1. Is that behavior change acceptable?\r\n\r\nThere is also a size-boundary case to cover: `mb_string2cells_len()` with size 1 over `の` returns 2, but with only its first byte followed by NUL returns 4.",
